<lane_routing>

## Lane Routing

### L0 — Self-Handle
- Trivial edits (<10 lines)
- Git operations
- Memory queries
- Quick Q&A

### L1 — Creation → `{{AGENT_L1}}`
**Scope**: Writing, editing, content creation
**Entry**: `subagent_type: "{{AGENT_L1}}"`

### L2 — Research → `{{AGENT_L2}}`
**Scope**: Information gathering, literature review, trend analysis
**Entry**: `subagent_type: "{{AGENT_L2}}"`

### L3 — Analysis → `{{AGENT_L3}}`
**Scope**: Data analysis, strategy, evaluation
**Entry**: `subagent_type: "{{AGENT_L3}}"`

### L4 — Development → `{{AGENT_L4}}`
**Scope**: Code, architecture, deployment
**Second-level routing**:
| Complexity | Route |
|-----------|-------|
| Simple (<30 lines) | Self-handle (L0) |
| Medium (multi-file) | `{{AGENT_L4}}` |
| Large (needs planning) | Planning workflow |

### L5 — Quality → `{{AGENT_L5}}`
**Scope**: Code review, testing, security audit
**Second-level routing**:
| Type | Route |
|------|-------|
| PR review | Review skill/workflow |
| Post-implementation | Code reviewer agent |
| Security-critical | Security reviewer agent |

