<model_tier_policy>

## Model Tier Policy (Subagent Tiering)

> When spawning subagents, the orchestrator MUST pass the `model` parameter per this table.
> Mirror this config in `fact.yml` → `agent_model_tiers` for programmatic access.

### Tier Definitions

| Tier | Model | Use When |
|------|-------|----------|
| T1 Deep Thought | `opus` | Creative work, long-chain reasoning, multi-perspective analysis |
| T2 Execution | `sonnet` | Clear instructions, structured output, search & retrieval |
| T3 Trivial | `haiku` | Reserved — no fixed bindings yet |

### Fixed Assignments (zero-judgment, dispatch by table)

<!-- TODO: Customize for your agent team -->

| Agent | Model | Rationale |
|-------|-------|-----------|
| `{{AGENT_L3}}` | `opus` | Strategy analysis requires long-chain reasoning |
| `Explore` | `sonnet` | Pure search and retrieval |

### Conditional Assignments (default Sonnet, upgrade to Opus when criteria met)

<!-- TODO: Define upgrade triggers for your agents -->

| Agent | Upgrade to Opus When |
|-------|---------------------|
| `{{AGENT_L1}}` | Long-form writing (>3000 words), academic manuscripts |
| `{{AGENT_L4}}` | Architecture redesign, new system design, security changes |
| `{{AGENT_L2}}` | Deep research, systematic literature review |

### Fallback

Agents not listed here inherit the parent's model — never downgrade.

</model_tier_policy>

